<title>THAILAND: Thai Jan-July rubber exports slip by six percent.</title>
<headline>Thai Jan-July rubber exports slip by six percent.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai rubber exports during the first seven months of this year dropped by six percent in value to 36.2 billion baht ($1.4 billion), commerce ministry officials said on Monday.</p>
<p>The officials attributed the fall to high stocks and a decline in demand. But they predicted a brighter outlook for the remainder of the year due to a recovery in demand.</p>
<p>Japan remained Thailand's most important market, followed by China and the United States.</p>
<p>Thailand exported 61.26 billion baht worth of rubber, mostly sheets, in 1995, a 47 percent rise from the previous year.</p>
<p>($1 = 25 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
